      "title": "Demonstration of an Automated Operation Planning System for ONGLAISAT CubeSat",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Nakamura R."
        },
        {
          "name": "Nomura S."
        },
        {
          "name": "Ishikawa A."
        },
        {
          "name": "Funase R."
        },
        {
          "name": "Nakasuka S."
        }
      ],
      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "The ONGLAISAT CubeSat, jointly developed by Taiwan Space Agency and the University of Tokyo, demonstrated high-resolution Earth imaging with Time Delay Integration technology. To support efficient operations with limited human resources, we developed an Automated Operation Planning System (AOPS) that generates satellite operation plans from high-level objectives. AOPS combines simplified models for rapid plan generation with high-fidelity simulations for validation and, if necessary, iterative repair. During the final phase of the ONGLAISAT mission, AOPS automatically generated and validated plans for imaging and downlink sessions, which were executed successfully on orbit. This demonstration confirmed the feasibility of automated plan generation for small satellites, improving both efficiency and reliability in real satellite operations.",
